  <keyword>nelson.mixin.SetGet</keyword>
  <short_description>Add set and get property access to a handle class.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>classdef MyClass &lt; nelson.mixin.SetGet</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>set(obj, name, value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>value = get(obj, name)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item><param_name>obj</param_name><param_description>a handle object of a class deriving from nelson.mixin.SetGet.</param_description></param_input_item>
    <param_input_item><param_name>name</param_name><param_description>a property name (char or string), or a cell array of names.</param_description></param_input_item>
    <param_input_item><param_name>value</param_name><param_description>the value to assign.</param_description></param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item><param_name>value</param_name><param_description>the property value.</param_description></param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Derive a handle class from <b>nelson.mixin.SetGet</b> to give it <b>set</b> and <b>get</b>
    methods for reading and writing properties by name.</p>
    <p><b>set(obj, name, value)</b> assigns a property; <b>set(obj, n1, v1, n2, v2, ...)</b> assigns
    several. <b>get(obj, name)</b> returns a property value; <b>get(obj)</b> returns a structure of
    all properties. Property names are matched case-insensitively.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Name-based property access.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="false"><![CDATA[classdef Widget < nelson.mixin.SetGet
  properties
    Width = 0
    Height = 0
  end
end
w = Widget();
set(w, 'Width', 100, 'Height', 40);
get(w, 'Width')]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
